# Enterprise-Grade Recommendation System with Deep Learning

## Project Overview
As a Senior Data Scientist at a digital platform, you are tasked with building an end-to-end Recommendation System for a scenario where real user interaction data is limited or unavailable. This project involves generating realistic synthetic data, building advanced models, and exposing them through an application layer.

## Key Features
* **Synthetic Data Generation:** Programmatic creation of 5,000+ users, 2,000+ items, and 100,000+ interactions using Faker and controlled probability distributions.
* **Multi-Model Approach:**
    * Baselines: Popularity-based, Collaborative Filtering (User/Item), and Matrix Factorization.
    * NLP: Content-based recommendations using TF-IDF on item descriptions.
    * Deep Learning: Neural Collaborative Filtering (NCF) using PyTorch with user/item embeddings.
    * Hybrid System: Scoring fusion combining collaborative, content, and deep learning models.
* **Evaluation & Explainability:** Tracking precision@K, recall@K, MAP@K, and NDCG@K while providing justification for recommendations.
* **Application Layer:** Implementation of either a FastAPI service or a Streamlit dashboard.

## Technical Stack
* **Synthetic Data:** Faker, NumPy
* **Data Processing:** Pandas
* **ML Recommenders:** Scikit-learn, Surprise
* **NLP:** TF-IDF
* **Deep Learning:** PyTorch
* **API/UI:** FastAPI / Streamlit
* **Version Control:** Git

## Project Structure
The repository must follow the directory structure below:
```
├── data/
│   └── synthetic_data/
├── notebooks/
│   ├── Advanced_EDA.ipynb
│   ├── Feature_Engineering.ipynb
│   ├── ML_Pipeline.ipynb
│   └── Deep_Learning_Model.ipynb
├── src/
├── models/
├── app/
└── reports/
```

## Mandatory Notebooks & Reports
* **Notebooks:** Advanced EDA, Feature Engineering, ML Pipeline, Deep Learning Model, Explainability & Governance.
* **Reports:** Data Risk Assessment, Cost Optimization, Governance & Fairness, and Final Business Recommendations.

## Submission Guidelines
* GitHub Repo Name: deep-learning-recommendation-system-{yourname}
* Notebook-only solutions will NOT be accepted.
* Either FastAPI or Streamlit is mandatory.
